  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Yi Tian Mountain, Heaven Overseeing Tower Lord names Sacred Feather City, Unbreakable Iron Fortress, Blood River Chariot, Nightmare Castle, Green Wave Pavilion, Weaving Cocoon Manor, and Golden Altar as seven Immortal Gu Houses Shadow Sect was forced to reveal.",
      "chapters": [
        1004
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_yi_tian_mountain",
        "char_heaven_overseeing_tower_lord",
        "house_sacred_feather_city",
        "house_unbreakable_iron_fortress",
        "house_nightmare_castle",
        "house_green_wave_pavilion",
        "house_weaving_cocoon_manor",
        "house_golden_altar",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page uses the Southern Border region field because the house is first named in the Yi Tian Mountain clash. Blood River Chariot is a mobile Immortal Gu House, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After another white fate attack from Heaven Overseeing Tower, Fang Yuan sees Unbreakable Iron Fortress, Blood River Chariot, and Nightmare Castle broken apart into fragments falling from the sky.",
      "chapters": [
        1005
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "destruction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Shadow Sect is beaten down and Fang Yuan takes leadership, the remaining resources include twelve Immortal Gu House construction plans. Blood River Chariot is named in that list with Nightmare Castle, Green Wave Pavilion, Weaving Cocoon Manor, Golden Altar, Sacred Feather City, and others.",
      "chapters": [
        1380
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shadow-sect-construction-plan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan builds an incomplete Immortal Gu House for joint battle with his subordinates, he takes reference from Blood River Chariot among many other Immortal Gu Houses, while the skeleton of the design is based on Graceful Chaotic Duel Stage.",
      "chapters": [
        1628
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "design-reference",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_graceful_chaotic_duel_stage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Crazed Demon Cave, Lady White Rabbit fields seven rank eight Immortal Gu Houses that Fang Yuan had assembled for his subordinates. Those houses are modified on the basis of Blood River Chariot and other Immortal Gu Houses, treated as partial innovations rather than wholly new designs.",
      "chapters": [
        2178
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "modified-descendants",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_crazed_demon_cave",
        "char_lady_white_rabbit"
      ]
    }
  ],
